    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, but the outlook remains strong at the top of the order. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premier play with an elite score of 83.29. Facing Bello, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% platoon edge and a strong BvP historical narrative, making him a high-floor candidate for multiple categories. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (75.77) and **Andy Pages** (67.30) are locked in as core starters against Nelson; both maintain strong efficiency scores, aided by favorable park factors and high-leverage spots in the order. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.76) faces a tougher test against Sale, he remains an essential start despite the SP_xERA hurdle, as his consistency in the heart of the order provides the stability we need to chase HR and RBI.\n\nNavigating the bottom of the lineup requires balancing marginal projections against our scarcity-driven strategy. **Brayan Rocchio** (52.14) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.86) provide just enough value to warrant starts, though both carry risk. **Jackson Merrill** is battling a difficult matchup against Wheeler, where his score is suppressed by the pitcher\u2019s elite ability to control the running game\u2014a direct hit to our secondary goal of securing SB. On the bench, **Miguel Andujar** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his score of 35.83 failed to clear the 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" due to an unfavorable platoon split. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined on the IL, our depth is thinner than preferred, placing additional pressure on fringe starters like **Coby Mayo** (50.44) to provide production against a middle-of-the-road arm in Bello. We are proceeding with this lineup but will monitor weather developments closely, as any shift in conditions could further erode the efficiency of our lower-scoring bats.",
